PE 842: Irrational Jumps / 无理跳跃

=== Problem Interpretation ===
'Irrational Jumps' involves processes where step sizes
are irrational numbers (√2, π, e, φ = golden ratio).

=== Beatty Sequences ===
Beatty sequence for α: ⌊α⌋, ⌊2α⌋, ⌊3α⌋, ...
Rayleigh Theorem: If 1/α + 1/β = 1 (α,β > 1 irrational),
then Beatty sequences for α and β partition ℕ.

Golden ratio φ ≈ 1.618033988750
Beatty partner: φ² = φ+1 ≈ 2.618033988750

Beatty sequence B_φ (first 15):
  ⌊1·φ⌋ = 1
  ⌊2·φ⌋ = 3
  ⌊3·φ⌋ = 4
  ⌊4·φ⌋ = 6
  ⌊5·φ⌋ = 8
  ⌊6·φ⌋ = 9
  ⌊7·φ⌋ = 11
  ⌊8·φ⌋ = 12
  ⌊9·φ⌋ = 14
  ⌊10·φ⌋ = 16
  ⌊11·φ⌋ = 17
  ⌊12·φ⌋ = 19
  ⌊13·φ⌋ = 21
  ⌊14·φ⌋ = 22
  ⌊15·φ⌋ = 24

